# UNHANDLED_ARM -- 3 rows. WGSLRenderer.code_for_op is {**CStyleLanguage.code_for_op, Ops.WHERE: ...}, so an op with no arm is a KeyError. The port answers UNHANDLED(Ops.X) -- a call to nothing, which cannot compile. The right totalization; see FINDING 2 for why the SAME exception is answered differently by FDIV.
code_for_op LOAD	REFUSE:KeyError	UNHANDLED(Ops.LOAD)	LANE
code_for_op MAX	REFUSE:KeyError	UNHANDLED(Ops.MAX)	LANE
code_for_op POW	REFUSE:KeyError	UNHANDLED(Ops.POW)	LANE

# MISSING_ARM -- 1 rows. Ops.FDIV is in ClangRenderer.code_for_op and NOT in WGSLRenderer.code_for_op (wgsl.py:60 merges the BASE's table, which has no FDIV), and the port adds one. wgsl.bend:441-448 records the same measurement and axes_hold() re-derives the set difference on every run.
code_for_op FDIV	REFUSE:KeyError	(A/B)	LANE

# WMASK_IS_GRAPH -- 6 rows. wgsl.py:18 is ((mask << shift_am) ^ 0xFFFFFFFF).cast(u32) and shift_am is SYMBOLIC, so CPython has no integer for a chosen shift. The oracle's cell reads GRAPH: and carries the two CONSTs CPython wrote; the port's is its own CONSTANT-FOLDING of the same expression.
