# TYPE_MAP_KEYERROR -- 1 rows. wgsl.py:62's type_map has NINE entries and render_cast/buf_map index it with brackets, so type_map[dtypes.double] RAISES. The port's catch-all arm answers UNHANDLED(dtypes.f64) -- a call to a dtype WGSL has no name for, which cannot compile. That is FINDING 2 FIXED: the arm used to answer the EMPTY STRING, a SPELLING no WGSL parser knows and the same silent-wrong-answer shape FDIV's fallthrough had. supported_dtypes keeps it unreachable from a real kernel. The name is `dt_name`'s, which is `DType.name`, which is why it reads `f64`.
